<?php require_once '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/shive/include/head.php'; ?>
<div class="shive" id="shive-containers">
  <p class="shive-hint">Auto-discovered from each container's bind mounts (<code>docker inspect</code> → <code>findmnt -T</code> → ZFS dataset). Override where discovery cannot resolve a path (e.g. paths through <code>/mnt/user</code> that do not exist on any pool) or tick <em>ignore</em> for containers that must never be stopped.</p>
  <p class="shive-hint"><b>Start order</b> decides which container comes back up first after a snapshot - lowest number first (0 = unspecified, sorted by name among equals). Containers are <b>stopped in the exact reverse order</b>, since whatever starts last depends on what came before it. Example: <code>paperless-redis = 10</code>, <code>paperless-ngx = 20</code> starts redis first and stops the app first. <b>Wait after start</b> pauses that many seconds before starting the next container, for a dependency that needs a moment to become ready; it is skipped after the last container. Both apply to every schedule - a dependency is a property of the containers, not of one schedule.</p>
  <div class="TableContainer">
  <table class="tablesorter shift shive-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Container</th><th>State</th><th>Discovered datasets</th><th>Bind mounts</th><th>Override datasets (comma separated)</th><th>Ignore</th><th>Start order</th><th>Wait after start (s)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody id="ctr-rows"><tr><td colspan="8">loading…</td></tr></tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p><span class="buttons-spaced"><input type="button" value="Save overrides" onclick="Shive.ctr.save()"> <input type="button" value="Rescan" onclick="Shive.ctr.load(true)"></span> <span id="ctr-msg" class="shive-hint"></span></p>
</div>
<script>$(function(){ Shive.ctr.load(false); });</script>
